I was having good fun with my chaotic elf wizard last night. The wizard 
was generated with a ring of polymorph control. Great I thought, now all 
I have to do is find a wand or ring of polymorph and I've got it made.

Sure enough, on lvl 3 was a large ring shop where I found a ring of 
polymorph. I figured I'd pick up the entire contents of the ring shop, 
don the ring, polymorph into a MMF and kill the storekeeper.

Unfortunately, after waiting a few thousand turns it never happened. So 
I went down a few levels, got the required funds, came back, and paid 
for the ring. One level later I got the opportunity to change shape and 
did. I went back, killed the shopkeeper, and took possession of the 
contents of the store.

There were stores on two other levels - an armor shop and a general 
store. I killed those storekeepers, too, since I had id'ed a scroll of 
identify and wasn't worried about store ids.

Now I had about 7000gp. I figured I'd go down the mines, eat the brains 
of any gnomes and dwarves I encountered, get even more gold from the 
foolish storekeepers on minetown, and do the protection racket. I was 
level 8 by that time.

A bookstore was on the minetown level. I promptly killed the proprietor 
and took his possessions. Naturally, I felt compelled to read the books. 
Compelled, until after trying to read one I got the message "you notice 
you have no gold!" Ouch - I had around 13,000gp! The only people left on 
the level were Izchak and the priest. I had determined that I was going 
to leave them alone.

I went back to the regular dungeon and found an altar dedicated to 
Thoth. Good deal, I figured, and decided to convert it. Unfortunately, 
Anhur was royally pissed at me for killing all those storekeepers and 
guards. Before I knew it, I was neutral. I had to sacrifice a bunch more 
to get into Thoth's good graces.

The big problem, though, was the fact that I was level 10 or so and 
hadn't gone past level 5 of the regular dungeon. Every single level was 
a pain. The shopkeepers were going to have the last laugh after all.

I tried to sacrifice to get magicbane and got Giantslayer instead - that 
told me that Magicbane had already been generated somewhere. But where? 
I wondered if it was in a bones file somewhere lower down. So I decended 
and finally got killed off by a xan and a winged gargoyle on level 16.

Yes, it was an annoying death, but I got a kick out of it when the list 
of monsters killed listed *6* shopkeepers!


